{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T22:06:50.276Z","author":"orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0d45976957f9ffc0b6cea979","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-web-qg8v"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Let Dependabot pm-github workflow bumps pass without a hand-edited version input"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The workflow-security policy required the deprecated pm-github-version input to equal the pinned release comment. Dependabot rewrites only the SHA and the comment, so every pm-github workflow bump failed. #286 and #287 sat open from 2026-11-01, and the scheduled sync ran pm-github 2026.10.19, whose gate refused a JavaScript regex literal in issue #218. pm-web-71et fixed the same deadlock once by hand. The reusable workflows have documented the input as deprecated (fallback for non-release commits) since 2026.10.2x. Fix: both callers pin pm-github 2026.11.02 without the input; the policy now refuses the input; the update-automation test proves a Dependabot-style SHA plus comment bump passes the real policy for both callers."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Chore"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["ci","dependabot","pm-github","workflows"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-02T22:06:50.276Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-02T22:06:50.276Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"orchestrator"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Both callers pin a pm-github release SHA with a matching release comment and no pm-github-version input; A SHA plus release-comment-only bump passes test/workflow-security.test.ts through the update-automation scenario; The scenario fails with the previous equality rule"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-web-71et","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-02T22:06:50.276Z","author":"orchestrator","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"34a25dbb0a5504aa5057434bfd3e64b8d77c40b7b32781e2661c43419f89f777","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"fed87cce6c6f5f5f66626711e79f7a0b02c903ca2452cefe980cec98c14d756a"}
